{"nodes": [{"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_bug_a_dic_expiry", "label": "Bug A DIC Expiry Without Manual Sourcing", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The reported RFQ was not blocked by code at all: the daily expiry job stopped running around 2026-07-25 and the token expired two days later; real code bugs found in the same job affect other RFQs.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_bug_b_po_published_leak", "label": "Bug B PO Published Leak Across Line Items", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "QCF data was aggregated per rfq_number, vendor_code and vendor_batch, so one item PO was joined onto every sibling row and the mapper overrode their status to PO Published; adding item_code to the aggregate narrowed 483 matched rows to 374, the 109-row gap being the leak.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_handle_expired_dic_review", "label": "handleExpiredDICReview", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_find_items_awaiting_dic_review", "label": "findItemsAwaitingDicReview", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Replaces the cron round-trip through the HTTP controller and scopes from the token row own columns rather than the JWT, so a malformed token is no longer fatal, and selects on status_dic IS NULL instead of status_milestone = 3, which is the real business condition.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_continue_without_deactivate", "label": "continue-without-deactivate Bug Class", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "is_active=false is written only on the success path, so one non-200 pins a token as expired-and-active forever and every later run reproduces the same failure; the same shape is copy-pasted across the CL, Management and CS handlers.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_build_rfq_qcf_agg_join", "label": "buildRfqQcfAggJoin", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_has_po_published", "label": "has_po_published Aggregate", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Both the label predicate and the status filter predicate must be narrowed together, otherwise a card is kept by the filter and then rendered under a different status.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_group_by_determinism", "label": "Aggregate Determinism Under Non-Strict GROUP BY", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "With ONLY_FULL_GROUP_BY absent, bare qcf columns in a multi-item group return an arbitrary row value; wrapping them in MIN and MAX makes the label, the ordering bucket and the filter agree.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_exclude_finished_items", "label": "excludeFinishedItems Finished-Work Guard", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "BA rule: an item that already carries a PO or is already iSourcing is finished, so close the token and do not process; a scope resolving to no rows also counts as finished, retiring orphaned tokens without sending email.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_cron_schedule_outage", "label": "2026-07-25 Cron Schedule Outage", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "sourcing_reason stamps show four independent stages stopping within 72 hours of each other against an 08:00 WIB run history, and 15 tokens the old selection would have found sit unprocessed, which rules out an empty-but-running job and points at the schedule.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_find_qcf_awaiting_approval", "label": "findQcfAwaitingApproval", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Gated on a null approval timestamp, po_number IS NULL and a milestone not in the finished set; excluding finished states rather than whitelisting pending ones keeps future milestones safe by default and stops completed purchases being converted back to manual sourcing.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_token_vendor_batch_scoping_weakness", "label": "Token vendor_batch Scoping Weakness", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Tokens are scoped by a vendor_batch that mutates as items advance, so any token issued at batch N becomes permanently unresolvable once items move to N+1; scoping tokens by item ids is the durable fix, closing dead tokens is only mitigation.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_cron_stage_cli_filter", "label": "Cron stage and rfq_number CLI Filter", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "runCronTasks already accepted stage and rfq_number options that no CLI could reach; parsing them lets a four-month backlog be drained in slices instead of firing every conversion, card and email at once.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_generate_dic_sourcing_link_token_hijack", "label": "generateDicSourcingLink Token Hijack", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The lookup matches on rfq_number and vendor_batch only, so one token row can be taken over across vendors and stages; deliberately left unfixed because scoping it would leave a CS token active and create a new DIC row, changing which expiry job fires.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_qcfa000731_anomaly", "label": "QCFA000731 Data Anomaly", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A QCF number generateNextQcfNumber cannot produce, on rows whose qcf milestone disagrees with their rfq milestone, indicating the rows were edited outside the application; investigated and cleared as not a release blocker.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_deactivate_tokens_scope_fix", "label": "deactivateTokens Scope Fix", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Unscoped, it closed every active token for the RFQ including DIC and vendor tokens for other batches; now scoped to the token vendor_batch and vendor_code.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_cs_loop_null_guard", "label": "CS Loop Null Guard", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "findOne returns null when a token RFQ row is gone and the property read sat outside any try/catch, so one orphaned token aborted the entire CS loop and silently skipped every remaining RFQ in that run.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_sequence_drift_guard", "label": "Sequence Drift Guard", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A payload vendor_sequence that narrows the selection to zero is treated as a real failure rather than nothing-to-do, because closing the token there would silently discard pending work.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_bug_a_dic_expiry", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_cron_schedule_outage", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_bug_a_dic_expiry", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_handle_expired_dic_review", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_handle_expired_dic_review", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_continue_without_deactivate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_find_items_awaiting_dic_review", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_handle_expired_dic_review", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/bugfix-plan-dic-expiry-and-po-published-leak.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_bugfix_plan_dic_expiry_and_po_published_leak_find_items_awaiting_dic_review", "target": "aige